  "coverage": [
    "Both actual platforms use normal helicopter packet validation/handler and real server pilot.150 accepted rockets alternate between fixed outer pod muzzles at5-tick intervals. Reload after75 shots preserves mode, sides and cooldown. Both75-round pods exhaust; switching back fires one Hellfire without refilling rapid inventory.",
    "All150 native first flight updates have speed6.25 blocks/tick, preserving source initial150 state then125 ordinary-update behavior and avoiding generic native .99 drag. No Hellfire target or flight state is attached.",
    "Additional real downward aim/fire packets at8-block aircraft altitude launch one rocket at ground infantry and one at a ground tank in separate scenes. Both actually lose health; aircraft/pilot remain intact and only one left-pod round is consumed. These observed damage values use the explicitly interim MC impact path, not source staged blast balance.",
    "Normal client input update and packet transport perform one switch to70mm, a held burst, release, switch back and one Hellfire. No server input injection, direct projectile spawn or ammo manipulation is used in client firing.",
    "Real client synchronized left/right stock and selected weapon HUD, actual fixed-pod muzzle positions, native rocket/impact/rotor/turbine playback, and exactly one hidden spent Hellfire rail are checked."
  ],
